  "description": "BIKLOX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C27 H32 Br3 Cl3 Er3 O14 1+,Cl1 1-,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.484-3.522 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.55-99.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er3L3(μ-OH)2Cl3(MeOH)3]Cl·3MeOH.",
